These Standard Terms & Conditions of Sale shall apply to any contract entered into by Nippon Paint Marine (Europe) GmbH and/or any of its associated companies; they form the only basis of any contract between the parties as defined herein, unless otherwise specifically agreed in writing by both parties. The Terms contained herein contain limitations of the liability of the Vendor, as defined.

1. Definitions & Contract Terms
The "Vendor" is Nippon Paint Marine (Europe) GmbH or any of its associated companies. The "Buyer" is the party contracted under the terms of any contract between the Vendor and that party for the supply of Products or Services. "Products" means the products described in the Vendor''s quotation. "Services" means any service or advice given by the Vendor, including technical guidance, specifications and instructions in connection with the Products. "Goods" means any combination of Products or Services. Unless other terms are expressly accepted in writing by the Vendor, the contract is on these Contract Terms to the exclusion of any other terms, whether or not endorsed upon, delivered with, or referred to in any purchase order or other document from the Buyer.

2. Quotations, Price & Payment Terms
A quotation does not create a contract until the Vendor despatches an acknowledgement of order. Only prices and terms communicated in writing are valid. Prices exclude duties, fees, taxes and VAT/sales taxes. Unless otherwise agreed in writing, payment is due within thirty days from the date of delivery (the Due Date), without deduction. The Vendor may charge interest at 5% above 3-month EURIBOR (minimum 5% p.a.) on overdue sums. If the Buyer is more than 30 days late in paying, or has ceased payments, or its financial circumstances have deteriorated, all sums under all agreements become payable immediately. Bills of exchange are only accepted as payment with the Vendor''s prior written consent. The Buyer shall indemnify the Vendor against all costs of recovering overdue sums.

3. Delivery, Returns, Storage, Risk & Title in the Goods
The Vendor will endeavour to deliver within the agreed time (or a reasonable time), but is not liable for loss or damage caused by delay, and delay does not entitle the Buyer to terminate unless it exceeds 180 days. Delivery is to the Buyer''s stated point (or ex-works if none is stated). Risk passes to the Buyer when the Goods leave the works. Title does not pass until the purchase price and all other sums due have been paid in full and any bills of exchange honoured, or until the Buyer resells the Products at arm''s length or processes them so they lose their original identity. The Buyer must insure the Products from delivery until title passes and hold any insurance proceeds on trust for the Vendor. No claim for non-delivery, shortage or damage is considered unless notified in writing within 7 days of delivery.

4. Guarantee and Exclusion Clauses
The Vendor is only liable if the Buyer has complied with the Contract Terms and the Vendor''s instructions. A merchant Buyer has no claim under guarantee unless recognisable defects are notified immediately in writing; other Buyers must notify obvious defects within 8 days of delivery. Claims that Goods are not of satisfactory quality must be made within 3 months of delivery; if justified, the Vendor will at its option replace the Goods, refund the price, or reimburse the Service fee. The Buyer indemnifies the Vendor against claims arising from use of the Goods. The Vendor is not liable for personal injury, death, loss or damage of any kind (other than death or injury from the Vendor''s own negligence), including loss of profits, except where such exclusion is not permitted by law.

5. Warranties
The Vendor warrants that on delivery the Products are made to its quality standards, free from defect, comply with its current published data sheets, and are suitable for the purpose for which they were prepared. The Vendor does not warrant fitness for any purpose other than as set out in its current data sheets or specifications. The Buyer is responsible for ensuring its staff and agents have and understand the relevant product data sheets, specification details and Health & Safety data.

6. Specification, Design & Promotional Material
A variation in specification or design that, in the Vendor''s reasonable opinion, does not affect suitability for the supplied purpose is not a breach of contract. The Vendor is not liable for any infringement of intellectual property rights by the Goods. Drawings, descriptive matter, catalogues and price lists do not form part of the contract and are not a warranty or representation. The Vendor will on request make available information needed to ensure the Goods are safe and without risk to health when properly used.

7. Set-off
The Buyer has no right of set-off, statutory or otherwise.

8. Force Majeure and Cancellation
The Vendor is not liable for delay or failure to perform caused by circumstances beyond its reasonable control (strikes, terrorist acts, war, supplier/transport/production problems, exchange fluctuations, governmental action, natural disasters). If such conditions persist beyond two months, the Vendor may cancel the contract for goods or work not yet supplied, without giving rise to any claim by the Buyer, who remains liable for Goods already delivered. If the Buyer cancels, extends, delays, or fails to take delivery at the agreed time, the Buyer must indemnify the Vendor for any resulting loss, including materials, plant, tools, labour and a profit margin.

9. Termination
The contract terminates immediately on the Buyer''s bankruptcy, insolvency, liquidation, or similar event, or on written notice by the Vendor if the Buyer suffers execution against its property, fails to perform its obligations, is unable to pay its debts, or ceases to trade. The Vendor''s rights (but not the Buyer''s) survive termination, and termination does not prejudice rights and duties accrued before it.

10. General
The Vendor may assign, sub-contract or sub-let the contract. Failure to enforce any term is not a waiver of it. Time is of the essence for the Buyer''s obligations. Notices must be in writing and are deemed delivered on the first working day after sending (or the fifth working day after first-class post within Europe). If any provision is invalid or unenforceable, the rest of the contract remains in effect to the maximum extent permitted by law.

11. Law & Jurisdiction
The contract is governed by and construed under the laws of Germany, to the exclusion of the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods (CISG). Disputes arising out of these Terms, including the validity of this arbitration clause, are decided by a court of arbitration under Hamburger Freundschaftliche Arbitrage (Hamburg friendly arbitration), without recourse to the public courts of law.', 1 where not exists (select 1 from public.phrases p where p.category = 'terms_and_conditions' and p.code is not distinct from 'standard' and p.text_en = 'STANDARD TERMS & CONDITIONS OF SALE OF NIPPON PAINT MARINE (EUROPE) GMBH AND ITS ASSOCIATED COMPANIES

